cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LEVI in your work, please cite it as below. Software and papers LEVI builds on are listed under references; cite those too where you use the matching component (see docs/REFERENCES.md)."
type: software
title: "LEVI: LeRobot Exploration, Validation & Integration"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
authors:
  - alias: "Koooki3"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Koooki3/LEVI"
url: "https://github.com/Koooki3/LEVI"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  LEVI is a bilingual workbench for robot demonstration and rollout data in the
  LeRobot dataset format: visualization, annotation of time segments and
  episode outcomes (by people or by a local vision-language model, always
  reviewed by a person), conversion of raw captures, quality review, training
  pool and training-manifest export, instance segmentation, RECAP value labels,
  and background labelling of robot evaluations. It is derived from the Hugging
  Face LeRobot Dataset Visualizer (Apache-2.0).
keywords:
  - robot learning
  - imitation learning
  - dataset visualization
  - data annotation
  - LeRobot
  - vision-language model
references:
  # upstream visualizer LEVI is derived from
  - type: software
    title: "LeRobot Dataset Visualizer"
    authors:
      - name: "Hugging Face"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot-dataset-visualizer"
    commit: "dc59887796fd41f37040c0df6b10e6f6a30a1854"
    date-released: "2026-07-24"   # author date of that commit, not a release
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: "Originally created by @Mishig25 (README); taken from huggingface/lerobot PR 1055."
